[break] closing-the-console-of-an-ended-program-is-an-error
rule: Hanging up on a program that has already ended is not an error. Two guards hold it since the step's review: a program that was waited for is not signalled at all (its id may be another's), and a group that has gone (ESRCH) is nothing to hang up. This breaks the second; the test's program was waited for, so the first stops it.
